{
  "_comment": "Per-system settings for tools/build_themes.py.  defaultScheme is the scheme an untagged page shows.  Give it a name only when the system defines that default at :root with no block of its own.  The build then makes it selectable by data-scheme.  renameAttrs maps a system's own attribute names onto the uniform data-mode and data-surface.  schemeClassPrefix is for systems that switch schemes with classes instead of attributes.  rootGuard names token files whose :root rules come after the scheme blocks and would override them on <html>.  backgroundVar names the page background variable when the page itself paints no solid background, so the browser check can tell light schemes from dark ones.  semantic overrides the source variable for any --rio-* token (see tools/semantic.py).  baseColorScheme declares a color-scheme for every scheme so nested light schemes do not inherit dark.  schemePatches fixes schemes that are broken in the original: each entry sets variables after the scheme block and says why.  _legibility lists maximum interaction tint percentages.  Generation reduces them when the palette needs more contrast headroom.",
  "_legibility": {"surfaceTint": 6, "hoverTint": 8, "pressedTint": 14, "selectedTint": 16},
